WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:13.150
What’s the deal, yo? This week we
keepin it on the DL with Invisible Man by

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.070
Ralph Ellison.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.140
Now when the narrator of dis book starts off
sayin he invisible, it

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.380
ain’t cuz he got super powers. It’s cuz
whenever people look at him, they only see

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.489
“their surroundings, themselves, and their
imagination.”

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:32.200
So this cat start reminiscing about back in
the day when his young self got “the honor”

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.010
of making speech in
front of some white folk. But before he do,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.730
The Invisible Man gotta throw down with some
bruthas and make a damn fool of himself as

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:44.410
entertainment. When it’s all said and done,
these crazy crackas throw him some change

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.620
for his education.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.600
In college, the narrator gotta
drive around a rich honkie named Norton. But

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.610
after showin him how black folk really live,
the Invisible Man gets expelled and ends up

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.920
grindin at a factory in New York.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.840
S’all good til one day sh** goes
hyphy at work and the narrator blacks the

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.000
fu** out.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.219
The Invisible Man hits the streets
of Harlem where he shacks up with some soul-sistah

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:10.920
named Mary, who heals his wounds and learns
him good on his black heritage.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.270
After the Invisible Man heal up,
some fools called the Brotherhood axe if he

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:21.600
wanna join an organization to help the oppressed.
The price- he kiss his name and his past goodbye.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.569
When Clifton, one of his
brotherhood boys, disappears, our boy goes

00:01:25.569 --> 00:01:32.490
looking for him but soon after see him get
capped by the 5- O. Rodney King preach!

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:36.399
So the narrator pours one out for
Clifton during his funeral, but the Brotherhood

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:39.149
start tweakin about him doin it without their
say-so.

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:44.060
sh** gets real when some thug named
Ras The Destroyer sparks a riot up in Harlem.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.300
This fool throws a god damn spear at the invisible
man, 

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.960
how the fu** you got a spear in harlem?

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.340
but our boy ducks it, picks it back up,

00:01:52.349 --> 00:01:59.349
and slangs it right in his grill. Then Inveezy
fall in to a sewer hole where the po-lice

00:01:59.349 --> 00:02:01.629
trap him. And he been chillin underground
ever since.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:39.200
Throughout this novel, Invisible
Man’s main game is finding a true identity

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.930
in a world full of phonies tryin to tell him
who he be. Whether it’s Emerson, Norton,

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.710
or Jack from 
the Brotherhood:

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.490
But only by defining himself can
the invisible man really break dem chains

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.600
and be free.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.510
So our boy try to find a gang of
other playas who fightin the same power. But

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.960
even the Brotherhood schemin to use the narrator
for they own purposes. They say they a gang

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.460
of liberators, but on the real, they really
just a bunch of oppressors. The Invisible

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.100
Man trying to find out who he is, but these
haters playin it raw and tell him to forget

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:19.970
his name and past.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.790
But how’s a brotha gonna cope with
all these haters rollin fake? Homie gotta

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.690
look at life with a new sense of awareness.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.380
Even though Invisible Man dealing
with some real street sh**, he learns to look

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.970
at life through through a COMIC FRAME. Like
his grandpappi say: “laugh to keep from

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:35.760
crying.”

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.840
Every single time this thug try to
change his life in order to stop being run,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.120
it ends up so far from what he intended that
it seems straight up absurd. For example,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.100
his speech at the beginning don’t give him
no respect, but it does give him a mouth full

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:50.900
of blood.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.480
When its all said and done, the
Invisible Man finally gets exactly what he

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.160
chasin. Wading through all dat absurd bullsh**
helps him find out who he truly is. Like my

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.100
main man Albert Camus once said:

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.860
In the end, our boy throws all
these fake haters to the wind, and say he

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.690
don’t need them to find his own identity.
So he buries himself underground, picks up

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:24.410
a pen, and defines himself through spittin
his story. That’s some heroic sh** right

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:24.849
thurr.

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:30.039
So define yo-self by pickin up some
of my swag. Tune in next week and get you

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:31.200
ass educated. Later!

